{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfu7WVNeAEwTbe78j8uY2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist. I haven't opened the dashboard to check how it renders, and I haven't confirmed the rule's query matches any documents.\n\n**What the data holds:** The sample web-logs data view has about 40 fields, with `timestamp` as its time field. The ones I used are `response`, `extension` and `bytes`, along with the `.keyword` variants of the first two. `response` is a string, so the 5xx check matches on `response.keyword`. Other fields describe the client (`clientip`, `agent`, `machine.os`), the request (`url`, `referer`) and geography (`geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `geo.coordinates`).\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-27a6a48c Web logs overview\" has four panels, with the time range set to the last 7 days:\n- Total requests, as a single number.\n- Requests over time, as a line chart.\n- Requests by response code, as a pie chart.\n- Average bytes by file extension, as a bar chart.\n\nIt's at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-27a6a48c-web-logs-overview-176f52bc3f46.\n\n**Alert rule:** \"EFF-27a6a48c 5xx spike\" (id `275b0cf4-256e-4532-a1b0-218730359537`) is an Elasticsearch query rule. It runs every minute and fires when more than 10 documents match a 5xx `response.keyword` (regex `5[0-9][0-9]`) in the last 5 minutes. The tool creates rules disabled, so I enabled it. It has no action connector attached, so when it fires it will only show as an alert in Kibana and won't notify anyone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":948,"cache_read_input_tokens":20310,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":948},"output_tokens":556,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null}